# SETUP's links between Servo Output and Motor Test: the owner's request of 2026-10-14 ("bug5"),
# which the C# does not have. At the foot of Mandatory Hardware > Servo Output, "Click here when
# done, to test your motor outputs", drawn as a web page's link, shows Optional Hardware > Motor
# Test; at the foot of Motor Test, "Click here to see your motor/servo outputs" shows Servo Output
# again.
#
# The claim: each link shows its page as that page's entry in SETUP's list does
# (crates/mp-gui/src/setup.rs, show_setup_page and page_link): the page chosen, the heading of a
# page under a closed one opened - Optional Hardware, for Motor Test - the page left deactivated
# and the page shown activated (ExtLibs/Controls/BackstageView/BackstageView.cs:428-523). Each
# link sits under its page's controls - Servo Output's under the sixteenth row, Motor Test's under
# Test all in Sequence - and is wholly in view at 1280x800 without scrolling: the layout guard
# counts every control cut off (layout.hidden), asked here along the way and, as every run asks
# it, at the end.
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760 started from tools/sitl/params/copter.parm, whose
# SERVO_32_ENABLE is 0 (sixteen outputs) and whose frame is a quad. Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/setup-links.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760
#
# or on the virtual display, leaving the desktop's pointer alone, as
#
#   tools/gui-headless.sh -- tests/gui/setup-links.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

screen setup
# The size the links must show at without scrolling: tests/layout.rs's smaller window.
window 1280x800
budget 15
# A first budget, set by hand until a passing run records one.
# A config.xml of its own, so the display view is Mission Planner's Advanced one, which lists
# both pages, and not whatever the machine running it chose.
env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml

# The vehicle first, and its parameters: SETUP lists both pages once every one is in
# (isConnected && gotAllParams, InitialSetup.cs:213-216, 315-318).
expect screen setup
expect vehicle.count > 0
expect params.held > 1000
expect setup.pages ~ ConfigRadioOutput
expect setup.pages ~ ConfigMotorTest

# Servo Output, chosen from the list.
click setup-page-ConfigMandatory
click setup-page-ConfigRadioOutput
expect setup.page ConfigRadioOutput
expect config.servo.active true
expect config.servo.rows 16
expect servo-to-motortest below servo-SERVO16_MAX
expect layout.hidden 0

# Its link: Motor Test, with Optional Hardware opened for it as the list opens the heading of a
# page under a closed one; Servo Output deactivated, Motor Test activated - its buttons built from
# the frame, as a choice in the list builds them.
click servo-to-motortest
expect setup.page ConfigMotorTest
expect setup.title Motor Test
expect setup.expanded ConfigMandatory,ConfigOptional
expect config.servo.active false
expect config.motortest.active true
expect config.motortest.count 4
expect motortest-to-servo below motortest-sequence
expect layout.hidden 0

# Motor Test's link: Servo Output again, its sixteen rows the page object's still, as a choice in
# the list keeps them; Motor Test hidden, both headings left open.
click motortest-to-servo
expect setup.page ConfigRadioOutput
expect setup.title Servo Output
expect config.motortest.active false
expect config.servo.active true
expect config.servo.rows 16
expect setup.expanded ConfigMandatory,ConfigOptional
expect servo-to-motortest below servo-SERVO16_MAX
